# Neon hands out two connection strings for the same database, and both are
# needed. The pooled one is what the app queries through; migrations need the
# direct one, because `prisma migrate` takes session-level advisory locks that
# a connection pooler can't hold — see `directUrl` in prisma/schema/schema.prisma.
#
# Both are on the Neon dashboard under Connect (the pooled host carries a
# "-pooler" suffix). Deploying: set BOTH on every Vercel environment, not just
# Production — a Preview build that can't see DIRECT_URL fails schema
# validation before it connects to anything.
DATABASE_URL="postgresql://user:password@host-pooler/dbname?sslmode=require"
DIRECT_URL="postgresql://user:password@host/dbname?sslmode=require"

# NO deployment migrates, production included. Migrations are applied by CI
# when a PR merges to main (.github/workflows/migrate.yml). They used to run
# in the Vercel build, gated to production, and that gate could not see a
# PROMOTION: promoting a preview reuses its already-built output, so the
# build command never re-runs and its migrations never apply.
#
# The Vercel build only CHECKS the schema now (scripts/check-schema.mjs, via
# apps/web/vercel.json) — a production build refuses while migrations are
# pending; a preview only warns, because an unmerged branch's own migration
# is legitimately not applied yet.
#
# There is no per-branch escape hatch. `ALLOW_PREVIEW_MIGRATIONS` was one and
# was documented here long after it stopped existing — it left with the
# build's migrate step, nothing has read it since, and setting it did
# nothing at all. To click through a branch that adds a model, apply its
# migration to the target database yourself and redeploy.
